    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0682" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/192A.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of
                        Honduras</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: The other day you
                    mentioned to me that you wanted to go to New York to sign the loan contract as
                    soon as <pb facs="0683" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/> this Department had concluded
                    its preliminary examination of that document. Therefore I hasten to write you
                    that we have now done so and to tell you at the same time that Mr. Conant, the
                    financial expert, has made his final statement that he regards the draft
                    contract in its present form as just and equitable and probably the best that
                    could be obtained for Honduras, and that we are likewise informed by a firm of
                    lawyers who were employed by the Department to examine it that they have reached
                    a similar conclusion, as will be set forth in a letter they are to send us in a
                    few days. Copies of these two letters are at your disposition.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
